cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  DOSEFIELD: a transparent 1-D deep-space radiation dose and
  shielding model with source-traceable constants
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata
  from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Zhanbolat
    family-names: Izbanov
repository-code: 'https://github.com/izbanovj3-prog/DOSEFIELD'
url: 'https://izbanovj3-prog.github.io/DOSEFIELD/'
abstract: >-
  A deterministic one-dimensional model of the deep-space
  galactic cosmic ray environment. A parametric GCR spectrum is
  transported in the continuous-slowing-down approximation through
  a shield of given areal density applied uniformly in every
  direction (spherical-shell geometry) and converted to absorbed
  dose and ICRP-60 dose equivalent at a point in water. Secondary
  particles produced in the shield are not transported; it is not
  a substitute for full radiation-transport codes. Every constant
  is taken from a cited primary source and no parameter is fitted
  to any validation target. Compared with NIST PSTAR proton
  stopping-power tables (1.55 percent maximum deviation above
  10 MeV across five low-Z materials) and with the MSL/RAD
  Mars-cruise measurement.
keywords:
  - space radiation
  - galactic cosmic rays
  - radiation shielding
  - dosimetry
  - stopping power
  - Bethe-Bloch
  - reproducible research
license: MIT
version: 1.0.1
date-released: '2026-10-17'
